{"parentUuid":"e2a7ed76-0b03-496f-9e69-e8abb272ec9b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"08993abf-0695-4a82-8cc6-e4d0c7458c7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mpnbct8F3XuXdPe7GG1y3Q","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding             e2468586c3 [credits-integration-2026-11]\n----\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/HomeSnapshot.hpp       |  68 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OnboardingModel.cpp    |  52 ++\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OnboardingModel.hpp    |  36 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp    | 562 +++++++++++-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.hpp    |  33 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/PrintHistory.cpp       |  47 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/PrintHistory.hpp       |  12 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/App.test.tsx     | 347 +++++++-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/App.tsx          |  46 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/bridge/protocol.test.ts |  20 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts      |  83 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/components/Glyphs.tsx   |   4 +\n .../JusPrin/HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx   | 539 ++++++++++++\n .../JusPrin/HomeUI/src/components/PrintHistory.tsx |  21 +-\n .../HomeUI/src/components/PrintReportForm.tsx      | 130 +++\n .../JusPrin/HomeUI/src/components/ProjectCard.tsx  |  21 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/history.ts       |  24 +\n .../GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/state/store.test.ts     |   3 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/state/store.ts   |  37 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/styles.css       | 966 +++++++++++++++++++++\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/styles.test.ts   |   2 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/tokens.ts        |  30 +\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Shell/GcodeHistoryRecorder.cpp     |   7 +\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Shell/GcodeHistoryRecorder.hpp     |   2 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/ShellController.cpp   |   4 +\n .../GUI/JusPrin/V1Import/WelcomeBackWindow.cpp     |   2 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/sources.cmake               |   4 +\n tests/agent/CMakeLists.txt                         |   1 +\n tests/agent/test_agent_bridge.cpp                  | 255 +++++-\n tests/agent/test_cloud_account.cpp                 | 146 ++++\n tests/agent/test_print_history.cpp                 |  77 ++\n tests/agent/test_project_state.cpp                 |  38 +-\n tests/agent/test_tool_coordinator.cpp              |  42 +\n tests/brand/test_brand_tokens.cpp                  |  23 +-\n tests/jusprin/CMakeLists.txt                       |   2 +\n tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp                   | 202 ++++-\n tests/jusprin/test_home_snapshot.cpp               |  56 ++\n tests/jusprin/test_onboarding_model.cpp            |  83 ++\n tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp                      | 212 ++++-\n 89 files changed, 5978 insertions(+), 124 deletions(-)\n----\n## 48ec76705d\nAdd JusPrin Cloud credits and the first-run path on Home\n\nThe app now shows and spends JusPrin Cloud credits, and a new install starts\non Home with a first-run path. This is steps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 of the credits\nplan on the app side. Step 3 (Chargebee, the served Account and pricing pages,\nv1 carry-over) is not here. It needs the gateway change on tsd-enterprise\nbranch claude/credits-ledger.\n\nOnboarding, ported from 8f4588beae and brought to the current boards:\n- Home walks through the welcome, importing presets from an OrcaSlicer install,\n  choosing a printer, and opening a project or the bundled example.\n- save_onboarding passed const char* to AppConfig::set, which saved every field\n  as \"true\". It now saves each value.\n- \"I don't have a printer here\" refused on a fresh install, because no vendor\n  was installed. It now installs Generic Klipper Printer and saves it under its\n  own name, as normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning.\n- The example opens handy_models/3DBenchy.drc. The earlier example file had\n  three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning.\n- An empty project is no longer listed on Home when its only history is\n  printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed.\n- The welcome-back window's kept-price box is hidden behind\n  V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER until step 3 ships.\n\nCredits:\n- Model pickers show each model's price and are greyed once the person has sent\n  a message in the chat. The account's balance shows as a ring with a hover\n  panel, and the composer offers \"Get more credits\" when a message can't be paid\n  for. A 402 from the gateway ends in a failed card.\n- Turns the app starts itself send X-JusPrin-Request: note and run on Expert\n  without changing the chat's model. RecordConversion turns one format's stored\n  turn into the other's, the same bytes each time, so provider caches still hit.\n- A Standard chat leaves out the picture tools and says so on the attachment\n  row, with a \"New Expert chat\" button.\n\nCost and rewards:\n- A turn that polls for its own slice is answered with busy, and the third\n  refused poll ends the turn. The note turn that reports the slice still runs.\n- Print history has a report form with a photo, and Home shows the credit line\n  when signed in to the account.\n\nTests: AgentUI Vitest (651) and HomeUI Vitest (130) with tsc, jusprin_tests\n(151), agent_bridge_tests (506), shell_theme_tests (14), brand_tokens_tests and\nthe shell harness default run (600 checks) and --fresh-example pass on macOS.\nThe real app ran the fresh-install example on an empty data folder, and three\nlive chats ran through a local gateway. Windows and Linux were not run.\ntests/shell/shell_harness.cpp also fixes three harness defects on macOS that\nwere there before this work: a null title bar menu in --print-history, page\nreads cut at about 1000 characters, and fake-printer control writes within one\nsecond being ignored.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EJ644FNDCPRA5S3703D1BX\n\n\n resources/jusprin/agent/protocol.json              |   4 +-\n resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json               |  25 +-\n resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json            |  20 +\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentConfiguration.cpp       |  30 +\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentConfiguration.hpp       |   5 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.cpp         | 162 +++-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.hpp         |  16 +-\n## 445ee541bd\nApply the final credit rules in the app\n\nKenneth reviewed the credits boards and changed the rules. Every credit is now\nthe same, a balance is one number of credits, and the app stops translating it\ninto messages.\n\n- The balance panel has one bar per lot, grouped by expiry, and bought credits\n  get a bar too. Workshop's bar adds \"Unused credits don't carry over.\"\n- Prices in messages stay only on the model menu and the stop card. The\n  first-month offer now reads \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key\n  stays free.\" Welcome-back reads \"750 credits a month.\"\n- The low-balance notice reads \"About 25 credits left\" at 25 credits or less on\n  any model that charges, once, with Get more credits and a close button. The\n  rounding to the nearest 5 is a fill-in, not Kenneth's.\n- \"New Standard chat\" and \"New Expert chat\" are gone, along with the host's\n  chatModel and draft path and the error details that fed them. A chat that\n  cannot be paid offers Get more credits only.\n- A picture in a Standard chat now shows as a warning on its chip, with Remove.\n- A new chat on the account starts on Expert while a first-month lot is live and\n  on Standard after it, as on board 6a. This was unbuilt until now.\n- Standard has no thinking picker, because its alias now has no efforts.\n\nFixed along the way: the two-line rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu\nrows have a fixed height. Vitest does not apply CSS, so a real-app screenshot\nfound it. No automated test guards it.\n\nNot done: the pricing page, the savings alert and the Account switch belong to\nlater steps and are not built. Open bug: on a Standard chat the app can show\n\"The automatic chat title could not be generated\", because the model sometimes\nanswers the message instead of writing a title (4 of 12 direct tries were too\nlong to use).\n\nTested: Agent page 654 tests, agent bridge 506, JusPrin 151. The real app ran\nagainst a local gateway with real keys: 0, 1 and 5 credits charged as intended on\na file-opened turn, a Standard message and an Expert message. The shell harness\nlast ran before the low-balance and report-limit changes. Windows, Linux and dark\nmode were not run.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZ6J03KW501EDCY1FCPDZR\n\n\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.cpp         |  48 ++++++---\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.hpp         |   3 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentProtocol.hpp     |   3 -\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ProjectStateDocument.cpp     |   4 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp     |   7 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/App.tsx         |  22 +---\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.test.tsx    |   2 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/WelcomeApp.test.tsx    |   2 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts     |   7 +-\n .../AgentUI/src/components/AgentConnection.tsx     |   2 +-\n .../AgentUI/src/components/AttachmentChip.tsx      |  24 ++---\n .../AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.test.tsx   |  84 ++++++++-------\n .../AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx        |  60 ++++-------\n .../src/components/Composer.credits.test.tsx       | 115 +++++++++++++--------\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Composer.tsx    |  43 ++++----\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/MessageList.tsx |  10 +-\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/WelcomeBack.tsx |   2 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/credits.ts      | 106 ++++++-------------\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css      |  37 ++++++-\n## 4af9ded841\nStop handling print reports that earn nothing\n\nKenneth removed the daily limit and the stop after invalid reports, so a report\nalways earns its 25 credits. The form's \"earned no credits\" screen, its two\nsentences and its Done button can no longer be reached, and neither can the\nnoReward field carried from the gateway through the host to the page.\n\nThe gateway side of this is on claude/credits-ledger in tsd-enterprise; the two\ngo together.\n\nTested: Home page 129 tests, agent bridge 506, JusPrin 151. Not run in the real\napp or the shell harness; a search of the harness found no use of what was\nremoved.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZ75WGREMC5K4S12BKD919\n\n\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/HomeHost.cpp             |  5 +----\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/HomeSnapshot.hpp         |  2 --\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/PrintHistory.cpp         |  5 ++---\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/App.test.tsx       | 16 ----------------\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts |  2 --\n .../HomeUI/src/components/PrintReportForm.tsx        | 20 +-------------------\n tests/agent/test_print_history.cpp                   |  5 -----\n tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp                     | 11 +++++------\n 8 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)\n## e2468586c3\nExpect no project card for a chat on an empty plate in --fresh-example\n\njusprin-newui now keeps an empty project in memory until it holds a model, so\na chat on an empty plate no longer saves the project or lists it on Home. The\nfresh-example harness check said the opposite and failed on the merged tree;\nit now expects the project to stay unlisted. The mode exits 0 with this change.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZY8VEHH504QM0TQG8CHYC\n\n\n tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp | 4 ++--\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"eb6939ec-0859-4f23-b116-13a3dbd1a1e8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:38:25.748Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding             