 +++-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.hpp         |  16 +-\n## 445ee541bd\nApply the final credit rules in the app\n\nKenneth reviewed the credits boards and changed the rules. Every credit is now\nthe same, a balance is one number of credits, and the app stops translating it\ninto messages.\n\n- The balance panel has one bar per lot, grouped by expiry, and bought credits\n  get a bar too. Workshop's bar adds \"Unused credits don't carry over.\"\n- Prices in messages stay only on the model menu and the stop card. The\n  first-month offer now reads \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key\n  stays free.\" Welcome-back reads \"750 credits a month.\"\n- The low-balance notice reads \"About 25 credits left\" at 25 credits or less on\n  any model that charges, once, with Get more credits and a close button. The\n  rounding to the nearest 5 is a fill-in, not Kenneth's.\n- \"New Standard chat\" and \"New Expert chat\" are gone, along with the host's\n  chatModel and draft path and the error details that fed them. A chat that\n  cannot be paid offers Get more credits only.\n- A picture in a Standard chat now shows as a warning on its chip, with Remove.\n- A new chat on the account starts on Expert while a first-month lot is live and\n  on Standard after it, as on board 6a. This was unbuilt until now.\n- Standard has no thinking picker, because its alias now has no efforts.\n\nFixed along the way: the two-line rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu\nrows have a fixed height. Vitest does not apply CSS, so a real-app screenshot\nfound it. No automated test guards it.\n\nNot done: the pricing page, the savings alert and the Account switch belong to\nlater steps and are not built. Open bug: on a Standard chat the app can show\n\"The automatic chat title could not be generated\", because the model sometimes\nanswers the message instead of writing a title (4 of 12 direct tries were too\nlong to use).\n\nTested: Agent page 654 tests, agent bridge 506, JusPrin 151. The real app ran\nagainst a local gateway with real keys: 0, 1 and 5 credits charged as intended on\na file-opened turn, a Standard message and an Expert message. The shell harness\nlast ran before the low-balance and report-limit changes. Windows, Linux and dark\nmode were not run.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZ6J03KW501EDCY1FCPDZR\n\n\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.cpp         |  48 ++++++---\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.hpp         |   3 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentProtocol.hpp     |   3 -\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ProjectStateDocument.cpp     |   4 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp     |   7 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/App.tsx         |  22 +---\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.test.tsx    |   2 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/WelcomeApp.test.tsx    |   2 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts     |   7 +-\n .../AgentUI/src/components/AgentConnection.tsx     |   2 +-\n .../AgentUI/src/components/AttachmentChip.tsx      |  24 ++---\n .../AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.test.tsx   |  84 ++++++++-------\n .../AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx        |  60 ++++-------\n .../src/components/Composer.credits.test.tsx       | 115 +++++++++++++--------\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Composer.tsx    |  43 ++++----\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/MessageList.tsx |  10 +-\n .../JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/WelcomeBack.tsx |   2 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/credits.ts      | 106 ++++++-------------\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css      |  37 ++++++-\n## 4af9ded841\nStop handling print reports that earn nothing\n\nKenneth removed the daily limit and the stop after invalid reports, so a report\nalways earns its 25 credits. The form's \"earned no credits\" screen, its two\nsentences and its Done button can no longer be reached, and neither can the\nnoReward field carried from the gateway through the host to the page.\n\nThe gateway side of this is on claude/credits-ledger in tsd-enterprise; the two\ngo together.\n\nTested: Home page 129 tests, agent bridge 506, JusPrin 151. Not run in the real\napp or the shell harness; a search of the harness found no use of what was\nremoved.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZ75WGREMC5K4S12BKD919\n\n\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/HomeHost.cpp             |  5 +----\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/HomeSnapshot.hpp         |  2 --\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/PrintHistory.cpp         |  5 ++---\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/App.test.tsx       | 16 ----------------\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts |  2 --\n .../HomeUI/src/components/PrintReportForm.tsx        | 20 +-------------------\n tests/agent/test_print_history.cpp                   |  5 -----\n tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp                     | 11 +++++------\n 8 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)\n## e2468586c3\nExpect no project card for a chat on an empty plate in --fresh-example\n\njusprin-newui now keeps an empty project in memory until it holds a model, so\na chat on an empty plate no longer saves the project or lists it on Home. The\nfresh-example harness check said the opposite and failed on the merged tree;\nit now expects the project to stay unlisted. The mode exits 0 with this change.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6EZY8VEHH504QM0TQG8CHYC\n\n\n tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp | 4 ++--\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2a7ed76-0b03-496f-9e69-e8abb272ec9b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"eb6939ec-0859-4f23-b116-13a3dbd1a1e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfTN9RNDURNCR6wC9VSP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sq81GbKffEwnyPfZrV3qKw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Projects/JusPrin && sed -n 1,60p credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md; echo ----; grep -n -i 'first-run\\|first run\\|onboarding\\|sign.in\\|welcome' pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md | head -30","description":"Read the handoff note for the credits branch and the plan's onboarding items"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3381,"cache_read_input_tokens":317314,"output_tokens":1076,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":454},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3381,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":317314,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3381},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Sq81GbKffEwnyPfZrV3qKw":{"command":"cd ~/Projects/JusPrin && sed -n 1,60p credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md; echo ----; grep -n -i 'first-run\\|first run\\|onboarding\\|sign.in\\|welcome' pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md | head -30","description":"Read the handoff note for the credits branch and the plan's onboarding items"}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgfTN8ur7NMvdD7y7Dxmw","requestRef":"0446f7b9-fa4c-465c-8af3-8e4fb8c959f6","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"45afb0fd-effe-4aef-b224-3513403c0405","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:38:26.974Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"distributed-snuggling-crane"}
{"parentUuid":"45afb0fd-effe-4aef-b224-3513403c0405","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"08993abf-0695-4a82-8cc6-e4d0c7458c7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sq81GbKffEwnyPfZrV3qKw","type":"tool_result","content":"# Handoff: build JusPrin Cloud credits and finish the first-run onboarding\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nWritten 2026-11-02 for a coding agent who has not seen the design sessions. This is a working doc: keep it untracked, never commit it, never add it to `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`. Kenneth tracks unfinished work by the untracked files in `git status`.\n\n## 1. What you are building, in one paragraph\n\nJusPrin 2 is a fork of OrcaSlicer with an in-app AI agent. The agent can run on the person's own API key (free, no account) or on JusPrin's hosted gateway (an Obico-server endpoint, `app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/…`, live in production since 2026-10-25). The gateway is about to start charging in credits: a Standard message costs 1 credit, an Expert message 5. People get 500 credits in their first month, can buy packs that never expire, or subscribe (Hobby $10, Workshop $20). This work adds the credit ledger and charging to the gateway, the balance, prices and pre-send checks to the app's composer, the Account and pricing pages, print-report rewards, and finishes the first-run onboarding flow that a month-old branch started. Nothing of this is built yet; the design is done and reviewed.\n\n## 2. Read these first, in this order\n\n1. `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` (same folder). The whole technical plan: ledger tables, the charging algorithm, the `/account` JSON, the 402 body, alias config, Chargebee, rewards, section 11 \"Order of work and tests\", section 12 \"Decisions still Kenneth's\". Build from it.\n2. `pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md`. Each point where a person meets credits, the five rules that apply everywhere, and the exact wording. When the plan and this doc disagree on words, this doc wins.\n3. The boards. Captures in `design-captures/credits-2026-11/` (one PNG per board, `credits-<board>-<slug>.png`, `-dark` variants where they exist). `MANIFEST.md` there lists every board with its canvas page and name; `CHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md` records why each board looks the way it does. The live canvas is the JusPrin v2 design artifact, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, at version 71. Figma is retired; do not design from it.\n4. `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md`, `fork-stewardship.md`, `design-system.md`. House rules; the ones that bite most often are repeated in section 7 below.\n\n## 3. Where the code lives\n\nYou run on Kenneth's Mac, the machine the design sessions ran on, so every path below is live. The three repositories are checked out here and on GitHub: the app at `~/Projects/JusPrin` (`git@github.com:TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin.git`, branch `jusprin-newui`), the gateway at `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/tsd-enterprise.git`, branch `master`, with `obico-server` as a submodule), and deployment at `~/Projects/ops` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/ops.git`). Other agent sessions work in these checkouts at the same time: make your own worktree for each repository you change, never reuse one you did not create, and touch nothing in the main checkouts themselves. The working docs this brief names sit untracked at the root of `~/Projects/JusPrin`; read them from there and leave them where they are.\n\n**App (this repository).** Branch `jusprin-newui` at `69780c7af4`, in sync with `origin`. Work in your own worktree and branch; never reuse another session's worktree.\n- Composer, pickers, attachments, Preferences page: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/` (`Composer.tsx`, `ModelPickers.tsx`, `AttachmentChip.tsx`, `Preferences.tsx`, `WelcomeBack.tsx`).\n- Host side of the agent: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` (`AgentHost.cpp` holds `chat_model_choice`, `use_chat_model`, `start_turn`; `ProviderAgent` sends the gateway headers and maps HTTP errors; `CloudAccount.cpp` and `ModelCatalog.cpp` hold the account's model list).\n- Home page and onboarding: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/` and `HomeUI/src/`. Preferences window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/`. The v1 import and the welcome-back window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/V1Import/`.\n- Tests: Catch2 under `tests/jusprin/` and `tests/brand/`; Vitest beside each TypeScript file; the shell harness under `tests/shell/` drives the built app without a screen.\n- Build: `cmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all -- -j4`. The Mac is shared by several agent sessions: check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja` first, one build per build directory, never restart a running build. Editing a CMake file rebuilds everything.\n\n**Gateway (tsd-enterprise).** Repository `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise`, branch from `master` (it moved 12 commits past the gateway merge, including the Python 3.12 / Django 5.2 bump), in your own worktree. The gateway is `web_ent/jusprin/v2/` (`aliases.py`, `upstream.py`, `gateway.py`, `stream.py`, `credits.py`, `auth.py`, `errors.py`, `views.py`, `urls.py`; tests in `tests/test_gateway.py` and `tests/test_aliases.py`, using the MockTransport injection the file already uses). `obico-server` is a git submodule: never stage or commit a submodule change. The local stack from the previous session is compose project `jusprin-cloud` on port 3434 (`docker-compose.local-ports.yml` in `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-cloud`, whose `LOCAL_TEST_ACCOUNT.txt` holds a test account), with `web_ent/scripts/jusprin/fake_upstream.py --port 8765` standing in for the model vendor. The session cookie is scoped to `.localhost`, so pass it as a header from scripts.\n\n**Deployment (ops).** `~/Projects/ops`: the alias ConfigMap is `tsd/prod/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml` and `tsd/stg/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml`. Staging is `https://app-stg.obico.io` and runs the same image as production. Production is live for real users: do not change it. For any `gcloud` or `kubectl` command, first run `gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com`, and stay read-only on production.\n\n## 4. Step 0: the onboarding branch\n\n`onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, Kenneth, 2026-10-06; `origin/onboarding-frontend-only` is identical) adds the local first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an existing OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer setup, open a project or the bundled example. Its commit message is a good spec of what it does and what it deliberately left out. It is 139 commits behind `jusprin-newui`.\n\nA dry-run rebase on 2026-11-02 conflicted in 18 of its 27 files. Expect to resolve `HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp`, `HomeHost.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.hpp`, `resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json`, `HomeUI/src/App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts`, `bridge/protocol.test.ts`, `state/store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp` and `test_home_snapshot.cpp`. Nine files apply cleanly, among them the three new ones (`OnboardingModel.cpp/.hpp`, `Onboarding.tsx`, `test_onboarding_model.cpp`). What changed underneath: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), the token sync (`7671e48504`). Most conflicts should be two additive hunks in the same place; keep both.\n\nAfter the rebase, bring the flow to the current design:\n- The canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth. The branch followed Figma frames; check each of its eight screens against the canvas before trusting its layout.\n- Boards 1a to 1d add the first-month offer as the headline on its own surface: \"Your first month: 500 credits\", under it \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", button \"Sign in for 500 credits\", \"Explore first\" below. 1a is the setup row in Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, 1b the welcome screen, 1c the welcome-back window the app already builds for a returning v1 user (signing in is the primary button there), 1d that window once a v1 subscriber has signed in. Never the word \"trial\"; no dollar figure.\n- The branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account go away: since 2026-10-23 every entry point to agent setup opens Preferences › Agent.\n- The branch left two paths unverified in the real app: a preset import that leaves some presets behind, and staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open. Show both before calling the step done.\n\n## 5. Then the credits work, in the plan's order\n\nSection 11 of the plan has the steps and their tests. Summary of what each needs and what it waits on:\n\n| Step | What | Waits on |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Gateway ledger and charging, the `slicer-basic` alias with image stripping, `/account`, the 402 body | Nothing. Start here on the server side. |\n| 2 | App: prices in the pickers, pickers greyed after the person's first message, app-started turns on Expert without fixing the chat's model, the attachment row's picture notice, the ring and hover panel, the pre-send check, the failed card | Step 1's `/account` and 402 shapes, which the plan fixes already. The webview that opens Account and pricing waits with step 3. |\n| 3 | Chargebee plans, add-ons, coupon, webhooks; the Account and pricing pages; v1-subscriber carry-over | Kenneth's decisions 12 (pages served into a webview, or built in the app), 10 (domain) and the open parts of 8 (when v1 subscribers move, how to word it). Do not start the pages until he has answered. |\n----\n9:- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n26:- **Your first month** (the sign-up grant, never called a trial): about $10 of credits (500), expiring one month after sign-in. During that month the 500 is all there is. **Free credits:** after the first month, every account not on a subscription, pack holders included, gets 50 ordinary credits a month.\n30:- **BYOK** (the person's own API key) stays free with no sign-in.\n58:**Desktop app.** `ProviderProfile.hpp` row `jusprin` (default model `slicer-1`, `account_sign_in` true) makes `ProviderAgent` send `X-JusPrin-Turn`, `X-JusPrin-Request` (reply or title) and `X-JusPrin-Chat`. `ProviderAgent::http_error` maps 402 to `quota_exhausted` with the text \"Your JusPrin account has used its Agent allowance for now. See your account for more.\" The Agent page gets `model_catalog` (per provider: models with `efforts`), `chat_model`, `account_status` (sign-in phase only) and `setup_keys` (the signed-in email). `ModelPickers.tsx` draws the per-chat model and effort pickers; `Preferences.tsx` has an `account` section. Print records (`ManufacturingHistory.hpp`, `GcodeRecord` with destinations and prints) live in the project file; nothing about them reaches the server.\n148:- **v1 subscribers** (decided by Kenneth 2026-11-02 on board 1c: \"grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"): people on `jusprin-unlimited-*` move to Hobby and keep their v1 price, $6.99 a month or $59.99 a year, for as long as the subscription stays active, and get the first-month 500 on top (boards 1c, 1d). In Chargebee: a plan change to `jusprin-hobby-monthly` or an annual Hobby plan with a per-customer forever coupon that holds the old price; the webhook grants 750 credits a term like any Hobby subscription. Open (the design session's fill-ins, decision 8): whether the move happens at sign-in to v2 or at the v1 term end, and how the page says that v1 was \"unlimited\" and Hobby is not. Twenty active v1 subscriptions, 15 annual and 5 monthly. Their v1 app is unaffected.\n176:`/jusprin/api/me/` stays as the sign-in check; the app calls `/account` after a sign-in check, after every completed or failed turn on the `jusprin` provider (one small GET, no streaming change), when the Preferences account section opens, and when the window regains focus after the person was sent to the browser to buy. A cheaper later step is a `X-JusPrin-Credits` response header on the stream start, but `AgentTransport` does not surface response headers today, so the GET comes first.\n258:## 9. Sign-in, accounts and the v1 free quota\n272:0. **Port the onboarding branch onto `jusprin-newui`** (app only; no dependency on the ledger). The branch `onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, 2026-10-06, same on `origin`) adds the first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer, open a project or the bundled example. It was built on `4389492239` and is 139 commits behind; a dry-run `git rebase jusprin-newui` on 2026-11-02 stopped with conflicts in 18 of its 27 files (`HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp/.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp/.hpp`, `home/protocol.json`, `App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts` and its test, `store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `test_home_host.cpp`, `test_home_snapshot.cpp`). The Home side changed under it: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), and the token sync (`7671e48504`). Rebase the one commit, resolve by keeping both sides' additions, then bring the screens to the current design: the canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth (Figma is retired), boards 1a to 1d put the first-month offer on the setup row, the welcome screen and the welcome-back window, and the branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account become the one setup flow in Preferences › Agent (decided 2026-10-23). Tests the branch carried (Home page Vitest, `test_home_host`, `test_home_snapshot`, `test_onboarding_model`, `test_brand_tokens`) must pass again; its two unverified paths (a partial preset import, staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open) still need to be shown in the real app.\n280:**Ready to hand off (assessed 2026-11-02):** steps 0, 1, 2 (except the Account and pricing webview), 4 and 5 are specified to the level a coding agent can build and test from this document plus the design doc and the boards. Step 3 waits on decision 12 (webview or in-app pages), decision 10 (the domain the app opens) and the open parts of decision 8 (when v1 subscribers move and how to word it); the webview part of step 2 waits with it. Decisions 1, 2, 4 to 7 and 13 to 16 have a recommended or placeholder answer written here and do not block the build. The handoff brief is `credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md`.\n295:8. **v1 unlimited subscribers:** decided, Hobby at their original price plus the 500 (section 4). Still open: the move at sign-in or at term end (recommend sign-in, since the v2 app is where they will be), and the wording about v1's \"unlimited\".\n305:Decided during the review (2026-11-02), so no longer here: a chat keeps its model; prices always say \"a message\"; the composer shows only a ring; a bar per expiring lot; \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page; no \"New Standard chat\"; the sign-in offer is the headline and the button names the reward; \"Your own API key\"; v1 subscribers keep their price on Hobby; the report button lives in Print history and on the Home card, not in the chat; boards live with their flows on the canvas; the cheap tier is \"Standard\" (not Basic, not Quick); a picture in a Standard chat is dropped and the attachment row says so; app-started turns run on Expert, free, without fixing the chat's model.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0cd1e880-6aa4-4ba3-aa3e-b3242785b285","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:38:27.050Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Handoff: build JusPrin Cloud credits and finish the first-run onboarding\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nWritten 2026-11-02 for a coding agent who has not seen the design sessions. This is a working doc: keep it untracked, never commit it, never add it to `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`. Kenneth tracks unfinished work by the untracked files in `git status`.\n\n## 1. What you are building, in one paragraph\n\nJusPrin 2 is a fork of OrcaSlicer with an in-app AI agent. The agent can run on the person's own API key (free, no account) or on JusPrin's hosted gateway (an Obico-server endpoint, `app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/…`, live in production since 2026-10-25). The gateway is about to start charging in credits: a Standard message costs 1 credit, an Expert message 5. People get 500 credits in their first month, can buy packs that never expire, or subscribe (Hobby $10, Workshop $20). This work adds the credit ledger and charging to the gateway, the balance, prices and pre-send checks to the app's composer, the Account and pricing pages, print-report rewards, and finishes the first-run onboarding flow that a month-old branch started. Nothing of this is built yet; the design is done and reviewed.\n\n## 2. Read these first, in this order\n\n1. `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` (same folder). The whole technical plan: ledger tables, the charging algorithm, the `/account` JSON, the 402 body, alias config, Chargebee, rewards, section 11 \"Order of work and tests\", section 12 \"Decisions still Kenneth's\". Build from it.\n2. `pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md`. Each point where a person meets credits, the five rules that apply everywhere, and the exact wording. When the plan and this doc disagree on words, this doc wins.\n3. The boards. Captures in `design-captures/credits-2026-11/` (one PNG per board, `credits-<board>-<slug>.png`, `-dark` variants where they exist). `MANIFEST.md` there lists every board with its canvas page and name; `CHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md` records why each board looks the way it does. The live canvas is the JusPrin v2 design artifact, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, at version 71. Figma is retired; do not design from it.\n4. `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md`, `fork-stewardship.md`, `design-system.md`. House rules; the ones that bite most often are repeated in section 7 below.\n\n## 3. Where the code lives\n\nYou run on Kenneth's Mac, the machine the design sessions ran on, so every path below is live. The three repositories are checked out here and on GitHub: the app at `~/Projects/JusPrin` (`git@github.com:TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin.git`, branch `jusprin-newui`), the gateway at `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/tsd-enterprise.git`, branch `master`, with `obico-server` as a submodule), and deployment at `~/Projects/ops` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/ops.git`). Other agent sessions work in these checkouts at the same time: make your own worktree for each repository you change, never reuse one you did not create, and touch nothing in the main checkouts themselves. The working docs this brief names sit untracked at the root of `~/Projects/JusPrin`; read them from there and leave them where they are.\n\n**App (this repository).** Branch `jusprin-newui` at `69780c7af4`, in sync with `origin`. Work in your own worktree and branch; never reuse another session's worktree.\n- Composer, pickers, attachments, Preferences page: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/` (`Composer.tsx`, `ModelPickers.tsx`, `AttachmentChip.tsx`, `Preferences.tsx`, `WelcomeBack.tsx`).\n- Host side of the agent: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` (`AgentHost.cpp` holds `chat_model_choice`, `use_chat_model`, `start_turn`; `ProviderAgent` sends the gateway headers and maps HTTP errors; `CloudAccount.cpp` and `ModelCatalog.cpp` hold the account's model list).\n- Home page and onboarding: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/` and `HomeUI/src/`. Preferences window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/`. The v1 import and the welcome-back window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/V1Import/`.\n- Tests: Catch2 under `tests/jusprin/` and `tests/brand/`; Vitest beside each TypeScript file; the shell harness under `tests/shell/` drives the built app without a screen.\n- Build: `cmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all -- -j4`. The Mac is shared by several agent sessions: check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja` first, one build per build directory, never restart a running build. Editing a CMake file rebuilds everything.\n\n**Gateway (tsd-enterprise).** Repository `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise`, branch from `master` (it moved 12 commits past the gateway merge, including the Python 3.12 / Django 5.2 bump), in your own worktree. The gateway is `web_ent/jusprin/v2/` (`aliases.py`, `upstream.py`, `gateway.py`, `stream.py`, `credits.py`, `auth.py`, `errors.py`, `views.py`, `urls.py`; tests in `tests/test_gateway.py` and `tests/test_aliases.py`, using the MockTransport injection the file already uses). `obico-server` is a git submodule: never stage or commit a submodule change. The local stack from the previous session is compose project `jusprin-cloud` on port 3434 (`docker-compose.local-ports.yml` in `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-cloud`, whose `LOCAL_TEST_ACCOUNT.txt` holds a test account), with `web_ent/scripts/jusprin/fake_upstream.py --port 8765` standing in for the model vendor. The session cookie is scoped to `.localhost`, so pass it as a header from scripts.\n\n**Deployment (ops).** `~/Projects/ops`: the alias ConfigMap is `tsd/prod/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml` and `tsd/stg/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml`. Staging is `https://app-stg.obico.io` and runs the same image as production. Production is live for real users: do not change it. For any `gcloud` or `kubectl` command, first run `gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com`, and stay read-only on production.\n\n## 4. Step 0: the onboarding branch\n\n`onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, Kenneth, 2026-10-06; `origin/onboarding-frontend-only` is identical) adds the local first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an existing OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer setup, open a project or the bundled example. Its commit message is a good spec of what it does and what it deliberately left out. It is 139 commits behind `jusprin-newui`.\n\nA dry-run rebase on 2026-11-02 conflicted in 18 of its 27 files. Expect to resolve `HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp`, `HomeHost.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.hpp`, `resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json`, `HomeUI/src/App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts`, `bridge/protocol.test.ts`, `state/store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp` and `test_home_snapshot.cpp`. Nine files apply cleanly, among them the three new ones (`OnboardingModel.cpp/.hpp`, `Onboarding.tsx`, `test_onboarding_model.cpp`). What changed underneath: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), the token sync (`7671e48504`). Most conflicts should be two additive hunks in the same place; keep both.\n\nAfter the rebase, bring the flow to the current design:\n- The canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth. The branch followed Figma frames; check each of its eight screens against the canvas before trusting its layout.\n- Boards 1a to 1d add the first-month offer as the headline on its own surface: \"Your first month: 500 credits\", under it \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", button \"Sign in for 500 credits\", \"Explore first\" below. 1a is the setup row in Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, 1b the welcome screen, 1c the welcome-back window the app already builds for a returning v1 user (signing in is the primary button there), 1d that window once a v1 subscriber has signed in. Never the word \"trial\"; no dollar figure.\n- The branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account go away: since 2026-10-23 every entry point to agent setup opens Preferences › Agent.\n- The branch left two paths unverified in the real app: a preset import that leaves some presets behind, and staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open. Show both before calling the step done.\n\n## 5. Then the credits work, in the plan's order\n\nSection 11 of the plan has the steps and their tests. Summary of what each needs and what it waits on:\n\n| Step | What | Waits on |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Gateway ledger and charging, the `slicer-basic` alias with image stripping, `/account`, the 402 body | Nothing. Start here on the server side. |\n| 2 | App: prices in the pickers, pickers greyed after the person's first message, app-started turns on Expert without fixing the chat's model, the attachment row's picture notice, the ring and hover panel, the pre-send check, the failed card | Step 1's `/account` and 402 shapes, which the plan fixes already. The webview that opens Account and pricing waits with step 3. |\n| 3 | Chargebee plans, add-ons, coupon, webhooks; the Account and pricing pages; v1-subscriber carry-over | Kenneth's decisions 12 (pages served into a webview, or built in the app), 10 (domain) and the open parts of 8 (when v1 subscribers move, how to word it). Do not start the pages until he has answered. |\n----\n9:- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the first month; the v1 welcome-back fill-ins; the print-report form details; alias ids `slicer-1` and `slicer-basic` with image stripping. **Dropped:** the reverse savings alert and board 7c; the month-end and 7-day expiry notices (rule 4 on board 0 loses them); the daily cap on free app turns; the thinking picker on Standard (Expert only). **Expiry:** every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end: first-month credits a month after sign-in, the free 50 a month after each grant, plan credits with the billing cycle.\n26:- **Your first month** (the sign-up grant, never called a trial): about $10 of credits (500), expiring one month after sign-in. During that month the 500 is all there is. **Free credits:** after the first month, every account not on a subscription, pack holders included, gets 50 ordinary credits a month.\n30:- **BYOK** (the person's own API key) stays free with no sign-in.\n58:**Desktop app.** `ProviderProfile.hpp` row `jusprin` (default model `slicer-1`, `account_sign_in` true) makes `ProviderAgent` send `X-JusPrin-Turn`, `X-JusPrin-Request` (reply or title) and `X-JusPrin-Chat`. `ProviderAgent::http_error` maps 402 to `quota_exhausted` with the text \"Your JusPrin account has used its Agent allowance for now. See your account for more.\" The Agent page gets `model_catalog` (per provider: models with `efforts`), `chat_model`, `account_status` (sign-in phase only) and `setup_keys` (the signed-in email). `ModelPickers.tsx` draws the per-chat model and effort pickers; `Preferences.tsx` has an `account` section. Print records (`ManufacturingHistory.hpp`, `GcodeRecord` with destinations and prints) live in the project file; nothing about them reaches the server.\n148:- **v1 subscribers** (decided by Kenneth 2026-11-02 on board 1c: \"grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"): people on `jusprin-unlimited-*` move to Hobby and keep their v1 price, $6.99 a month or $59.99 a year, for as long as the subscription stays active, and get the first-month 500 on top (boards 1c, 1d). In Chargebee: a plan change to `jusprin-hobby-monthly` or an annual Hobby plan with a per-customer forever coupon that holds the old price; the webhook grants 750 credits a term like any Hobby subscription. Open (the design session's fill-ins, decision 8): whether the move happens at sign-in to v2 or at the v1 term end, and how the page says that v1 was \"unlimited\" and Hobby is not. Twenty active v1 subscriptions, 15 annual and 5 monthly. Their v1 app is unaffected.\n176:`/jusprin/api/me/` stays as the sign-in check; the app calls `/account` after a sign-in check, after every completed or failed turn on the `jusprin` provider (one small GET, no streaming change), when the Preferences account section opens, and when the window regains focus after the person was sent to the browser to buy. A cheaper later step is a `X-JusPrin-Credits` response header on the stream start, but `AgentTransport` does not surface response headers today, so the GET comes first.\n258:## 9. Sign-in, accounts and the v1 free quota\n272:0. **Port the onboarding branch onto `jusprin-newui`** (app only; no dependency on the ledger). The branch `onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, 2026-10-06, same on `origin`) adds the first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer, open a project or the bundled example. It was built on `4389492239` and is 139 commits behind; a dry-run `git rebase jusprin-newui` on 2026-11-02 stopped with conflicts in 18 of its 27 files (`HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp/.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp/.hpp`, `home/protocol.json`, `App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts` and its test, `store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `test_home_host.cpp`, `test_home_snapshot.cpp`). The Home side changed under it: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), and the token sync (`7671e48504`). Rebase the one commit, resolve by keeping both sides' additions, then bring the screens to the current design: the canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth (Figma is retired), boards 1a to 1d put the first-month offer on the setup row, the welcome screen and the welcome-back window, and the branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account become the one setup flow in Preferences › Agent (decided 2026-10-23). Tests the branch carried (Home page Vitest, `test_home_host`, `test_home_snapshot`, `test_onboarding_model`, `test_brand_tokens`) must pass again; its two unverified paths (a partial preset import, staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open) still need to be shown in the real app.\n280:**Ready to hand off (assessed 2026-11-02):** steps 0, 1, 2 (except the Account and pricing webview), 4 and 5 are specified to the level a coding agent can build and test from this document plus the design doc and the boards. Step 3 waits on decision 12 (webview or in-app pages), decision 10 (the domain the app opens) and the open parts of decision 8 (when v1 subscribers move and how to word it); the webview part of step 2 waits with it. Decisions 1, 2, 4 to 7 and 13 to 16 have a recommended or placeholder answer written here and do not block the build. The handoff brief is `credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md`.\n295:8. **v1 unlimited subscribers:** decided, Hobby at their original price plus the 500 (section 4). Still open: the move at sign-in or at term end (recommend sign-in, since the v2 app is where they will be), and the wording about v1's \"unlimited\".\n305:Decided during the review (2026-11-02), so no longer here: a chat keeps its model; prices always say \"a message\"; the composer shows only a ring; a bar per expiring lot; \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page; no \"New Standard chat\"; the sign-in offer is the headline and the button names the reward; \"Your own API key\"; v1 subscribers keep their price on Hobby; the report button lives in Print history and on the Home card, not in the chat; boards live with their flows on the canvas; the cheap tier is \"Standard\" (not Basic, not Quick); a picture in a Standard chat is dropped and the attachment row says so; app-started turns run on Expert, free, without fixing the chat's model.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sa